NOTICE

PhoenixEye is a local device-diagnostics utility designed for authorized
security testing, education, and personal device audits. It is intended to
be run only against devices and networks you own or have explicit written
permission to test.

The architectural inspiration for this project comes from the open-source
"Hound" tool by TechChip (https://github.com/techchipnet/hound). No original
source files from that repository are bundled, modified, or redistributed
here. All code in this repository was written independently and is released
under the MIT terms above.

Portions of the chat UI styling are derived from the public "Simple Chat"
CSS template by Masud Rana, distributed under the MIT License.

The authors of PhoenixEye do not condone, support, or take responsibility
for any use of this software that violates applicable laws, infringes on
the privacy of others, or is performed without the informed consent of the
device owner. Users are solely responsible for ensuring their use complies
with all applicable local, national, and international regulations.

